From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: add RTL8192XB to the RTL8852C family checks

The RTL8192XB is a single-band 2.4 GHz member of the RTL8852C family.
Realtek's driver programs its MAC, PCIe and security engine with the
8852C register layout, so add rtw89_is_rtl8852cx() and use it where the
core checks for the RTL8852C.

The differences follow Realtek's driver and its per-cut patch table:
- it has no band 1, so the band-1 DMA index clear stays 8852C only;
- SIFS_MACTXEN_T1 is 0x40;
- the scheduler prebackoff time is not tied to the TX partial mode;
- the L1.2 vmain and Gen2 forced-IB patches apply to all cuts;
- the PCIe EQ, 160 MHz GI/LTF and ER SU rules stay 8852C only.

The firmware is built from the 8852C 0.27 code line, so it takes the same
feature and coex version thresholds.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
